<title>UK: World Bank sets 125 mln stg August 1999 bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank sets 125 mln stg August 1999 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by joint lead managers Nikko and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT    125 MLN STG   COUPON     7.0	 MATURITY    10.AUG.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.71    PAY DATE   L10.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.125     REOFFER    99.71     SPREAD	+5 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  1.00</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.0 PCT AUGUST 1999 GILT</p>
<p> NOTES	UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED</p>
<p>		LAUNCHED OFF THE ISSUER'S GLOBAL MULTI CURRENCY</p>
<p>		NOTE PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
